# Continuous-branch double Y-fork demo for paper figure (连续分支双分叉演示)
# 
# Geometry: thick trunk → fork1 → continuing child B1 + side C1 → fork2 on B1
# → continuing child B2 + side C2. Two successive binary forks along main
# continuation chain.
# Radii: parent ≈ B1 ≈ B2; side branches C1, C2 thinner but not extreme.
#
# This SWC demonstrates the convex-hull junction flaw in the continuous-branch
# case with TWO successive forks: the hull wraps bulkily around both smooth
# continuations, swallowing the gentle crotches and losing the continuous-tube
# appearance, while the Y-Fork method preserves the main continuation as a
# bent pipe with two clean side ports.
#
